## Task #17 — strengthened trio-leak pin.
##
## Source: docs/specs/system/zero_rust_stdlib_classes.spec.md (B5).
##
## Resolves `FooBar` through the `std.foobar.FooBar` namespace path —
## the same shape every other stdlib type uses (`std.io.File`,
## `std.fs.OpenOptions`, `std.net.TcpStream`). Pre-Task-17 this fails
## because the hand-maintained STD_SUBMODULES list in
## `resolve/stdlib/mod.rs` does not include `foobar`, so `std.foobar`
## is not a known submodule even though `library/std/foobar/src/lib.rx`
## is bootstrap-loaded. After Task #17 derives STD_SUBMODULES from
## BOOTSTRAP_FILES basenames, this resolves automatically.
use std.foobar.FooBar

def main
  let x = FooBar.new(42)
  let v = x.get
  if v == 42
    puts "ok"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
